title: Dorm_Desk
tags: interactable dorm
---
<<if $dressed>>
    Anin: I'm all ready. Time to go.
<<else>>
    Anin: I should hurry.
    -> Get dressed
        <<jump Dorm_Dressing>>
    -> Do nothing
        // Closes the dialogue.
<<endif>>
===

title: Dorm_Dressing
tags: cutscene dorm
---
<<set $dressed to true>>
Narrator: Anin showers, does her makeup in a rush, and puts on her graduation uniform.
Narrator: She stops in front of the mirror. For a moment, she just looks at herself. A single tear slides down her cheek before she even notices it. She doesn't know why.
<<quest_update "graduation_day" "Go to the auditorium.">>
===

title: Dorm_Door
tags: interactable dorm
---
<<if $dressed>>
    Anin: Leave the room?
    -> Yes
        <<minimap_show>>
        <<minimap_set_marker "Auditorium">>
        // Temporary: goes to the school map until the Auditorium scene exists.
        <<scene_load "SchoolMap" "Morning">>
        // <<scene_load "Auditorium" "Morning">>
        // <<jump Auditorium_Arrival>>
    -> Later
        // Closes the dialogue.
<<else>>
    // Blocked until the player picks "Get dressed" at the desk.
    Anin: I can't go out like this.
<<endif>>
===

title: Auditorium_Arrival
tags: cutscene auditorium
---
// Start node of the Auditorium scene. It only plays once, so coming back to the auditorium later skips it.
<<if $lila_intro_done>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Narrator: Anin expects rows of graduates in matching uniforms. Instead, every student around her is in their regular uniform. She is the only one dressed for graduation.
Anin: (under her breath) Isn't graduation today? Am I still dreaming? Why is everyone in their regular uniform?
<<companion_join "Lila">>
Lila: Well, well. Looks like someone couldn't wait to graduate. What are you cosplaying, the season finale of a high school slice-of-life anime?
Narrator: A few students snicker. Even Lila is looking at her like she's lost it.
Anin: (thought) What is going on? What's the date today? Why hasn't the ceremony started?
-> What's the date today?
    Anin: What's the date today?
    Lila: It's still December 10th, dumbass. And we've got a whole festival to enjoy.
-> Isn't today graduation day?
    Anin: Isn't today graduation day?
    Lila: Sure is, for you, apparently. Congrats, you're the only graduate. The rest of us are still stuck on December 10th, dumbass, and we've got a whole festival to enjoy.
Lila: Stop messing around and let's go find Dira and Kirana. We're enjoying this festival together, no excuses!
Lila: Dira's probably in the classroom doing next semester's homework for fun. Lead the way, boss.
<<quest_strike "graduation_day">>
<<quest_start "find_the_gang" "Find Lila, Dira, and Kirana.">>
<<quest_check "find_the_gang" "Lila">>
<<set $lila_intro_done to true>>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Auditorium_BasketballStudent
tags: interactable auditorium npc
---
<<if $talked_basketball>>
    Narrator: He's too busy dribbling to notice you.
<<else>>
    <<set $talked_basketball to true>>
    Basketball Student: Oh, hey Anin. Why are you wearing a graduation uniform?
    -> Just wanted a fresh look.
        Anin: Just wanted a fresh look.
        Basketball Student: It's unusual to see you wearing something different, haha. Is this Lila's doing?
        Lila: Sybau.
    -> I thought today was graduation. Weird, haha.
        Anin: I thought today was graduation. Weird, haha.
        Basketball Student: Everyone can't wait for graduation, so we can finally be free of this school.
    // Placeholder: both answers end with the "training" line for now.
    Basketball Student: I've got some training to do. See you, Anin.
<<endif>>
===

title: Auditorium_NeighborStudent
tags: interactable auditorium npc
---
<<if $talked_neighbor>>
    Student Next Door: Let's make the most of the festival, Anin!
<<else>>
    <<set $talked_neighbor to true>>
    Student Next Door: Morning, Anin. What's with the graduation uniform?
    -> Nothing, I just wanted to.
        Anin: Nothing, I just wanted to.
        Student Next Door: It does look good on you. I can't wait to graduate and go to uni. How about you?
    -> It's all Kirana's fault.
        Anin: It's all Kirana's fault.
        Student Next Door: Having you and Kirana as my neighbors made high school a lot more interesting. Any plans after graduation?
    // Both answers end with a question about after graduation. The answers live in their own node:
    // a second group of options written right below the first would merge into one five-option wheel.
    <<jump Auditorium_NeighborStudent_Plans>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Auditorium_NeighborStudent_Plans
tags: auditorium npc
---
-> Mm, yeah. Seems like everyone can't wait to graduate.
    Anin: Mm, yeah. Seems like everyone can't wait to graduate.
-> I don't know. I haven't made any plans yet.
    Anin: I don't know. I haven't made any plans yet.
-> I just want to keep enjoying school while there's still time.
    Anin: I just want to keep enjoying school while there's still time.
===

title: Auditorium_Door
tags: interactable auditorium
---
<<if $lila_intro_done>>
    Anin: Head to the classroom?
    -> Yes
        Narrator: Anin decides she has either lost her mind or is about to. Either way, she and Lila head to their classroom.
        // The Classroom scene's Intro plays Classroom_Enter as its start node.
        <<scene_load "Classroom" "Morning">>
    -> No
        // Closes the dialogue.
<<endif>>
===

title: Classroom_Enter
tags: cutscene classroom
---
// Start node of the Classroom scene. It only plays once, so coming back to the classroom later skips it.
<<if $classroom_intro_done>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Narrator: Dira sits alone by the window, writing something in a notebook. She doesn't look up until Lila bursts through the door.
Lila: DIRAAA! LOOK AT THIS DUMBASS! Someone graduated early today. Cum laude, too, for outstanding academic performance.
Narrator: Dira laughs softly behind her hand, careful not to hurt Anin's feelings.
Dira: Anin, why are you wearing your graduation uniform? Are you really that nervous about graduating?
-> I don't know... I guess I didn't get enough sleep.
    Anin: I don't know... I guess I didn't get enough sleep.
-> I had a really weird dream last night.
    Anin: I had a really weird dream last night.
Dira: Ahaha. I thought Kirana was pranking you. Where is she, by the way?
Lila: That's what we came to ask you. I thought she was with you.
Dira: She asked to borrow my book, then just ran off with it. I have no idea where she is now.
<<set $found_dira to true>>
<<quest_check "find_the_gang" "Dira">>
Anin: Let's look for her at...
-> The cafeteria
    <<set $clue_location to "cafetaria">>
-> The music room
    <<set $clue_location to "music_room">>
<<minimap_set_event_marker $clue_location>>
<<set $classroom_intro_done to true>>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Classroom_GroupStudents
tags: interactable classroom npc
---
Anin: (thought) They're discussing the new K-drama episode. Wait, why did they suddenly switch to theology??
===

title: Classroom_Desk
tags: interactable classroom
---
Anin: Good old desk. I'll miss you after graduation.
