title: Classroom_Door
tags: interactable classroom
---
<<if $classroom_intro_done>>
    Anin: Leave?
    -> Yes
        <<minimap_show>>
        // Minimap shows the "!" event icon at the cafeteria or music room. This also introduces the minimap events.
        // Temporary: goes to the school map until the cafeteria and music room scenes exist.
        <<scene_load "SchoolMap" "Morning">>
        // <<scene_load $clue_location "Morning">>
    -> No
        // Closes the dialogue.
<<endif>>
===

title: Clue_ObservantStudent
tags: interactable clue npc
---
// Same NPC and dialogue in the cafeteria and the music club room. Only the background changes.
<<if $found_clue>>
    Observant Student: Good luck finding her!
<<else>>
    Dira: Oh, isn't that the Observant Student? She notices everything. I saw her talking to Kirana before she left. Maybe we can ask her.
    Observant Student: Hi, everyone! Oh, that looks good on you, Anin.
    Anin: Thanks.
    -> Do you know where Kirana is?
        Anin: Do you know where Kirana is?
    -> We were looking for Kirana. Any clue?
        Anin: We were looking for Kirana. Any clue?
    Observant Student: Oh yeah, she was rushing toward the school park with a red book in her hand. Weird to see Kirana holding a book.
    Anin: School park, noted. Thanks!
    <<set $found_clue to true>>
    // <<minimap_set_marker "SchoolPark">>
    Narrator: The three of them hurry over.
    // The SchoolPark scene's Intro plays Park_Intro as its start node.
    // <<scene_load "SchoolPark" "LateMorning">>
<<endif>>
===

title: Park_Intro
tags: cutscene park
---
// Start node of the SchoolPark scene. It only plays once, so coming back to the park later skips it.
<<if $park_intro_done>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Narrator: The park is packed shoulder to shoulder with festival-goers.
Dira: There are way too many people. We'll never find Kirana in this sea of people.
Lila: Not even Moses could part this crowd. C'mon, Anin, use your spider-sense. You two have been glued together for years.
Dira: Let's just look for my book. It's bright red, so it should stand out.
<<search_mode_start "red_book">>
<<set $park_intro_done to true>>
<<give_control>>
===

title: Park_Takoyaki
tags: interactable park
---
Vendor: Takoyaki, takoyaki! Come treat your mouth to our special sauce!
Anin: (thought) Ball-shaped dough filled with octopus. The sauce is what makes it good, savory with umami from the bonito flakes. The perfect snack after a long day.
===

title: Park_CottonCandy
tags: interactable park npc
---
Student with Cotton Candy: Hmmmm, so sweet and fluffy. This might be the greatest human invention ever.
-> Sorry to bother you, but have you seen Kirana around here?
    Anin: Sorry to bother you, but have you seen Kirana around here?
-> Where did you get that cotton candy?
    Anin: Where did you get that cotton candy?
Student with Cotton Candy: Hmmmm, it's sticky.
Anin: (thought) This guy is too busy with his cotton candy.
===

title: Park_DartGame
tags: interactable park npc
---
Student at Dart Game: If I win this, I can get the plushie that Student X wants.
Anin: (thought) Is he the one with a crush on Student X?
===

title: Park_RedBook
tags: interactable park npc
---
<<if $found_redbook>>
    Bookworm Student: Good luck finding Kirana!
<<else>>
    <<set $found_redbook to true>>
    Anin: There you are! Where have you b...?!
    Narrator: The student turns around. It isn't Kirana.
    Bookworm Student: Oh, hey, Anin. What's up?
    Narrator: The three of them freeze.
    Dira: Sorry! We thought you were Kirana, since you have my book.
    Bookworm Student: Oh, it's yours? Kirana gave it to me. She said she has a copy of this one somewhere in her room.
    -> She doesn't even read her school books.
        Anin: She doesn't even read her school books.
    -> There is zero literature in her room.
        Anin: There is zero literature in her room.
    -> If she ever read a book, the world would end tomorrow.
        Anin: If she ever read a book, the world would end tomorrow.
    Anin: So where is she now?
    Bookworm Student: She left right after she gave me the book. Maybe check the photography club? I saw her talking to someone with a camera.
    Anin: Thanks.
    <<search_mode_end "red_book">>
    <<minimap_set_marker "PhotographyClub">>
    // The player walks to the photography club on the school map. Its Intro plays PhotographyClub_Cutscene as its start node.
<<endif>>
===

title: PhotographyClub_Cutscene
tags: cutscene club
---
// Start node of the PhotographyClub scene. It only plays once, so coming back to the club later skips it.
<<if $found_kirana>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Narrator: The room is cluttered with props and backdrops, with a few photo sessions running at once. It's quieter here. The first thing they see is Kirana, posing in front of the photo backdrop.
Lila: KIRANUY! We've been looking all over for you!
Narrator: Lila sprints over, and lands squarely in the frame just as the club member snaps the shutter.
Kirana: You ruined my photoshoot!
Lila: I made your photo a thousand times prettier. Also, behold: the graduate.
-> Call me Anin-senpai from now on.
    Anin: Call me Anin-senpai from now on.
-> You'll have to find a new roommate tomorrow.
    Anin: You'll have to find a new roommate tomorrow.
Narrator: Kirana bursts out laughing.
Kirana: Okay, but seriously, why are you dressed like that?
-> It's your fault for leaving without me.
    Anin: It's your fault for leaving without me.
-> If only someone had woken me up this morning.
    Anin: If only someone had woken me up this morning.
Kirana: Sorry, sorry! I couldn't wait to see what everyone was doing for the festival. So what's the plan? Just wander around and have fun?
Lila: I mean, yeah, that's the plan. But first, a group photo. Who knows when we'll get another chance to be photographed by the greatest photographer in the world?
Narrator: She shoots the club member a look.
<<set $found_kirana to true>>
<<quest_check "find_the_gang" "Kirana">>
<<quest_complete "find_the_gang">>
Photography Club Member: (flatly) Okay. Everyone say "cheese."
Narrator: The four of them squeeze into the frame. The shutter clicks.
// Flash, then the world stays frozen through Loop1_End until <<loop_end>> releases it.
<<freeze_frame>>
<<jump Loop1_End>>
===

title: Loop1_End
tags: cutscene
---
Narrator: Lila was right. There would never be a better time than right now, because time itself had broken.
Narrator: Tomorrow would come, and it would still be December 10th, the day before graduation. So would the day after that, and the day after that, for Anin and for everyone at school.
Narrator: The girls spent the rest of the day wandering the festival, and that night they slept soundly, ready for whatever tomorrow would, or wouldn't, bring.
<<loop_end 1>>
===
